# Plan: Screen-news WebSocket subscriptions

Feature: `speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.specify`
Architecture: `speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.architecture.md`
Database schema: `speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.database-schema.md`
Tasks: `speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.tasks`
Contract IDs: `CID-MBOOK-WS-SCREEN-NEWS`, `CID-MBOOK-NEWS-SETTINGS-SCREEN`
Status: Implemented and accepted for the authorized T00-T10/T12 scope on 2026-10-09. All three backend module compiles and isolated standalone SQL acceptance passed; iOS was statically reviewed only. T11, working/live database changes and deployment remain deferred. See the tasks file's execution acceptance for checksums, evidence limits and user-directed residual authentication risks.

## 1. Scope

In scope:
0. Prerequisite: mbook gets the mbooks controller → service → DAO and `ApiResponseFactory` layering (task T00). Routes and responses do not change.
1. An iOS `MenuVC` toggle that reads and writes the logged-in user's screen-news subscription.
2. The subscription API: dalogin `GET`/`PUT /login/admin/newsSettings/screen` forwards to mbook `GET`/`PUT /mbook-1/rest/news-settings/screen`.
3. mbook `/mbook-1/ws` identifies each socket by `deviceId` and sends screen news only to subscribed users.
4. mbooks screen add, update and delete publish `eventType` after commit.
5. mbooks `/mbooks-1/ws` stops broadcasting screen news.
6. `news_settings` uniqueness: one row per `logins_id`.
7. Database Engineer delivers a separate **full standalone schema-and-data RC SQL dump**, derived from an untouched copy of the actual working dump, with required isolated full-import/insertion evidence. A migration script is not the final product. Delivered as `k8infra/mysql_8/screen_news_standalone_rc.sql`, using the user-confirmed login source and the explicitly accepted older `mysql_8/book.sql` supplement.

Out of scope:
- Auth of simple-service-webapp `GET /webapi/myresource/admin`.
- AngularJS UI, toast/presentation redesign, `newsTrending` and other categories.
- `/news/{user}` and user notifications (`ios-users-notifications`).
- Outbox, new tables, CHECK/DEFAULT constraints and other schema changes.
- Persistent socket-client registry, polling, account-deletion policy.
- Fixing the existing `user/` and `device/` filter regexes (see note in §3).

## 2. Decisions

| ID | Decision |
|---|---|
| D1 | Subscription API name: `news-settings` with sub-resource `/screen`. |
| D2 | iOS calls dalogin only via `loginPath("admin/newsSettings/screen")`. Extend the existing `AdminServlet` with the exact mapping `/admin/newsSettings/screen`; no new servlet. Keep `performTask` and existing session/token/activation checks unchanged. Only the active handler branches to new `callNewsSettingsAndRespond` with its existing attributes. Activation `"S"` uses unchanged `handleActivationRequired`/`prepareActivationRequired` and account-profile call, returning legacy 300 and activation headers with no settings call or mutation. Existing `/admin` behaviour and responses remain unchanged. |
| D3 | dalogin forwards with the same headers as `AdminServlet`: `user`, `token2` (`deviceSessionManager.getToken2(deviceId)`) and `TIME_` (session creation time), plus `X-Token`, `Ciphertext` and cookies via `RequestFilter`. |
| D4 | The mbook `CookieFilter` and `CiphertextFilter` path conditions also match `^/?(rest/)?news-settings/screen$`. |
| D5 | Active users come from simple-service-webapp `GET /simple-service-webapp/webapi/myresource/admin`, a proxy of dalogin's in-memory `/login/activeSessions`. No DB query is made for active users. |
| D6 | The recipient check runs at send time. When a different user logs in on a device, the next event uses that user's subscription. |
| D7 | Delivery requires exactly `newsScreening == "yes"`. A missing row, `no`, NULL or any other value means no delivery. |
| D8 | Schema: `news_settings.logins_id` becomes `INT NOT NULL` and gains `UNIQUE (logins_id)`. PK and FK are unchanged. |
| D9 | The WS client ID is the iOS `currentDeviceId()`, sent as `?deviceId=` on every connect and reconnect. |
| D10 | Unsubscribing keeps the socket open. Resubscribing resumes delivery on the same socket. |
| D11 | mbook is refactored first, following `.ai/skills/mbooks-controller-dao-flow/SKILL.md`. `BookController` and `BookingHandlerImpl` are replaced by `AccountController`/`NewsController` with `AccountService`/`NewsService`. New mbook code (news-settings, recipient lookup) uses the services. The existing 5 endpoints keep identical status codes, header names/values and semantic JSON body shape (field types, nullability). JSON key order and equivalent escaping are not contract requirements. |
| D12 | USER-CONFIRMED SQL deliverable: full standalone schema + seed/data dump, not migration. Database Engineer identifies/preserves the working source, generates a new RC, matches actual final models/DAO writes and records required disposable MySQL import/insertion checks before T12. No execution is authorized by this documentation turn. |

## 3. Contracts

### 3.1 iOS → dalogin

```
GET  /login/admin/newsSettings/screen            -> 200 {"enabled":true|false}
PUT  /login/admin/newsSettings/screen  {"enabled":true|false}  -> 200 {"enabled":<committed value>}
```

- Headers: the existing `SessionHeaderProvider` set (`X-Token`, `Ciphertext`, `X-Device`) plus the session cookie.
- The existing `AuthFilter` `/admin/*` mapping protects the route; no filter change. No session returns its existing 502 error and is not forwarded. Keep AdminServlet's `processRequest`, `performTask`, existing checks and handler token2 lookup/exception handling unchanged; add no token/token2/activation-null or session-identity guards. Only `handleLoginForActivedUser` selects the new news-settings method versus the current account-profile method using its existing attributes. POST on the news path returns 405 with `Allow: GET, PUT`. Existing `/admin` GET/POST responses remain unchanged.
- Activation `"S"` for news GET/PUT reuses unchanged `handleActivationRequired`: `prepareActivationRequired` sets **300**, `Response: S` and `X-Token`, then `callServiceAndRespond` retrieves/writes the existing account-profile body. No news-settings call or mutation occurs. This body is not `ScreenNews`; iOS uses existing 300 activation response handling (`APIClient` throws `AppError.activationRequired` before settings decoding).
- For active news requests only, dalogin passes the mbook status and body through unchanged, including the unrelated filter 403 in §3.2.

### 3.2 dalogin → mbook

```
GET  /mbook-1/rest/news-settings/screen
PUT  /mbook-1/rest/news-settings/screen   Content-Type: application/json  {"enabled":bool}
Headers: user, token2, TIME_, X-Token, Ciphertext, Cookie: XSRF-TOKEN=...
```

| Case | Status | Body |
|---|---|---|
| GET, row `yes` | 200 | `{"enabled":true}` |
| GET, row `no` or missing row | 200 | `{"enabled":false}` |
| GET, row value not `yes`/`no` | 500 | `{"error":"invalid_news_setting"}` |
| PUT valid | 200 | `{"enabled":<bool written>}` |
| PUT body missing `enabled` or not a boolean | 400 | `{"error":"invalid_body"}` |
| `user` header unknown in `logins` | 404 | `{"error":"user_not_found"}` |
| Filter mismatch (Ciphertext ≠ token2, XSRF) | 403 | existing filter body |
| DB error | 500 | `{"error":"db_error"}` |

- PUT upserts by `logins_id`. It writes only `newsScreening` (`yes`/`no`), keeps the existing row id, and commits before responding.
- Body fields `user`, `loginId` and `deviceId` are ignored.

Note: mbook filters use `UriInfo.getPath()`, which includes `rest/`. D4's regex accepts both forms. The existing `user/` and `device/` patterns are left unchanged.

### 3.3 WebSocket `/mbook-1/ws?deviceId=<id>`

- `@OnOpen`: a missing or blank `deviceId` closes with `CloseReason.CloseCodes.VIOLATED_POLICY`. Otherwise the session is registered under `deviceId`. A device may have several sessions.
- `@OnClose`/`@OnError` remove that session only.
- Message (text JSON): the existing `AddMovie` fields plus `"eventType":"created|updated|deleted"` and `"category":"screening"`.

### 3.4 Event

`AddMovie.eventType` (String) is added in both mbook and mbooks. A null `eventType` on consume means `created`. The topic `ios-movies-notifications2` is unchanged.

## 4. Delivery algorithm (mbook `KafkaMoviesListener`)

For each record:
1. Deserialize to `AddMovie`, then call the injected `NewsService.saveNewEvent(event)`, preserving the existing transaction and persistence ordering.
2. Call `admin` once per record. Build `deviceId -> set(user)` from the JSON array (`deviceId`, `user` keys); skip blank values.
3. For each registered `deviceId`:
   - The device must map to exactly one user. Zero users or more than one means skip.
   - Resolve the user via `AccountService.getUser(user)`; skip sentinel id 0. Load the subscription via `NewsSettingsService` using `logins.id`, and deliver only when the stored value is exactly `"yes"`.
   - Send to every open session for that device. A send failure removes that session only.
4. If the admin lookup fails or returns non-200, nothing is sent for this record. Log it and continue to the next record.

## 5. Implementation order

Before SQL changes: the user confirms `k8infra/mysql_8/Dump20260524.sql` is the latest working dump and includes events. Record that confirmation and the file checksum, and preserve a separate untouched byte-for-byte copy including user dirty content before generating the RC. The repository dump's recorded contents cover `login_`; the canonical `mysql_8/book.sql` is separate evidence for `book`, not proof that the dump exhaustively covers that schema or its current data. Map actual coverage for the standalone RC without merging the `login_`/`book` boundary or treating source identity as unconfirmed; this confirmation does not authorize a live export. Original-source snapshots still precede any implementation-file edits (T-preflight).

0. Prerequisite: mbook layering refactor (T00). No behaviour change.
1. Database Engineer generates a new full standalone RC (T01; planned path `k8infra/mysql_8/screen_news_standalone_rc.sql`, no file created now) from a separate untouched copy of the user-confirmed latest working dump. Preserve full source schema/data, unrelated objects, triggers/routines, PK/FK behavior and the `login_`/`book` split; include only approved bounded changes. RC alone must import into a fresh empty target without source/migration/previous-schema dependencies. The dump's repository contents cover `login_` and do not include `book`; identify the actual `book` schema/data source needed for the standalone RC, without assuming canonical `book.sql` proves current data or inventing seeds. The migration snippet/runbook is intermediate/rollout reference, never the final product or an RC import dependency.
2. mbook: `NewsSettingsController`, `NewsSettingsService`, DAO methods, filter regex.
3. dalogin (Backend Engineer, protected auth/session contract): `NewsSettings` client interface, `ServiceClient` methods, exact `/admin/newsSettings/screen` mapping and GET/PUT dispatch. Add only an active-handler branch and `callNewsSettingsAndRespond`, plus `AdminResponses.newsSettingsDownstream`; leave `performTask`, the inactive handler and account-profile method unchanged. Existing AuthFilter `/admin/*` mapping needs no edit.
4. mbook: active-session client, WS registry, gated delivery.
5. mbook/mbooks: `AddMovie.eventType`; mbooks publish for update/delete; mbooks `KafkaListener` stops broadcasting.
6. iOS: WS `deviceId` query, `BackendServices` news-settings calls, `MenuVC` toggle.
7. Static dry run, actual model matching, application compile-only gate and required bounded isolated SQL import/insertion checks (T10), after all edits.
8. Final Backend Engineer review (T12), including model alignment and SQL acceptance evidence.

Steps 2 and 4 depend on step 0. Steps 1, 3 and 6 are independent of step 0. Steps 2–3 and 6 are independent of step 4. Step 5 depends on step 4.

## 6. Working rules

- Do not run commands between edits. Stage large replacements in session `files/*.txt`, then apply them with view/edit.
- Before the first edit, deletion or rename of each existing implementation file, capture its full current on-disk content verbatim in session `files/originals/<repo-relative-path>.txt`. Include user-owned uncommitted content; do not substitute git HEAD or overwrite snapshots. Mark new files as `new` in the execution record. Originals are reference/rollback artifacts, not staged replacements; capture any newly scoped file before touching it.
- Never overwrite the working dump or its untouched copy; generate the separate RC from that preserved source and record source/copy/RC paths and checksums. All SQL execution waits until edits and static model matching are complete.
- Do not commit, push or deploy without explicit approval.
- The initial documentation-only authorization was subsequently superseded by explicit user authorization for T01-T10 and T12 implementation and isolated SQL acceptance. T11, working/live database changes and deployment remain deferred. Telemetry is disabled.

## 7. Validation gate (after all edits)

| Check | Command / method |
|---|---|
| Schema/model mapping | Database Engineer compares RC with confirmed working copy and canonical `mysql_8` scripts; maps real final entities/API models and DAO writes to tables/columns, checking actual/implicit `@Entity`/`@Table`/`@Column`/`@JoinColumn`, types/lengths, nullability, ids/generation, defaults, FKs, uniqueness and exact String yes/no. See T10 for source paths and acceptance details; never invent columns from wire DTOs. |
| Required isolated SQL acceptance | After all edits and static mapping, Database Engineer imports RC alone into a fresh empty disposable MySQL 8 target; verifies full source data/object preservation and FK integrity, detects duplicate/NULL/orphan owners and invalid preferences without silent cleanup, then runs representative valid insertion/update/re-read and duplicate/NULL/missing-FK rejection checks with constraints enabled. Check generated ids/defaults, trigger behavior, unchanged unrelated preferences and affected event writes. Use real ORM roundtrip only if feasible without application startup/Java tests; otherwise matching parameterized SQL is required and must be labeled SQL evidence, not ORM/API runtime evidence. Record version/SQL mode, isolation, final RC checksum and results. |
| Compile | `./mvnw -q -DskipTests compile` in `mbook-quarkus`, `mbooks-quarkus` and `dalogin-quarkus`. |
| Refactor | Static inspection finds no `BookingHandlerImpl`/`BookController` references in mbook source; compare the T00 changes against its preservation list. |
| iOS | Static review only; no `swiftc` or `xcodebuild`. Swift compilation is not covered by this gate. |
| Dry run | Read-only comparison of original snapshots with final contents, including new/deleted files. Routes, filter regex, headers and JSON keys match §3; AdminServlet remains minimally adapted and activation `"S"` returns existing 300 without subscription mutation. |
| Final review | T12: Cinemas Backend Engineer reviews final changes, successful compiles, actual model alignment and Database Engineer's SQL import/insertion evidence for the final RC. Fix findings, rerun affected compiles; regenerate RC and repeat static matching/fresh-target SQL checks if impacted, then obtain approval. |

Application validation in T10 remains compile-only: no Java/runtime/Swift tests, application service startup or deployment. The sole additional execution allowance is the **required bounded isolated SQL import/insertion harness**, not migrations against working/live DBs. Existing dumps use `CREATE DATABASE`/`USE`, qualified names and definers: choosing another default schema on a shared server is unsafe. Prefer a disposable instance with no live connectivity/credentials, retaining canonical names there; alternatively require reviewed complete retargeting and grants confined to disposable schemas. MySQL startup is permitted only for that harness. A safe target/harness is a prerequisite, never assumed.

Dependency chain: T-preflight source identity/untouched copy → T01 separate RC generation → T10 static matching against final T02/T07 models/DAO → isolated full import/insertion validation → T12 final review. SQL failures require scoped fixes, RC regeneration and retest on a fresh target, never hand repairs to fake a pass. Compiles are run first, then failures triaged. Completion requires executed SQL acceptance and T12 approval; static checks alone cannot accept the RC.

Runtime check (existing RestAssured login→admin smoke test, then manual testing; no new tests, no news-settings automation) waits for T10 and T12 and requires separate approval. Deployment also requires separate approval.
T11 includes no working/live migration or RC restore; any rollout needs distinct explicit authorization. The existing `04-db-migration-runbook.md` remains rollout reference, not authority to bypass these gates.

## 8. Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Existing duplicate/NULL owners, orphan FKs or invalid preferences block RC acceptance | File inspection or separate disposable source import; explicit owner-approved reconciliation decision, no silent cleanup or live writes. |
| The admin lookup adds latency per event | One call per record, not per device. |
| `DAO.updateScreen` swallows commit failures | Make failure visible to `VenueController`, and publish `updated` only on success. |
| MySQL DDL commits implicitly; dump schema directives can target the wrong DB | Disposable isolated import only; no transaction rollback dry-run claim, no restore over working/live schemas. Reverse DDL is intermediate rollout reference, not an RC dependency. |
| Full dual-schema source coverage or a safe isolated SQL harness is not yet evidenced | User confirmation resolves working-dump identity and event presence, not exhaustive coverage. Preserve the exact `login_`/`book` split and reconcile the separate canonical `book.sql` evidence with the confirmed source; an isolated harness remains required for SQL acceptance. |
| The T00 refactor changes a response (e.g. `profilePicture` missing when set, or appearing as `null` when unset; a lost `User`/`Device` header) | T10 diff review against the preservation list. T11 RestAssured login→admin smoke covers `/user/` through dalogin; `profilePicture` is checked manually. |
